===Prepare to return the Coreflame of Worldbearing{{subst:void|<!--104061201-->}}===
{{Mission Description|type=trailblaze|location=Vortex of Genesis|The music for the curtain call has begun to play, and the show nears its end... But before that, the silent audience will offer you their applause, celebrating your completion of this tragedy, commemorating your path toward the next tragedy.<br />Toward the tragedy he yearns for.<br />Either banish the audience from this mythical theater, or let this performance become the swan song of all creation.}}
{{Dialogue Start}}
----
:'''Hysilens:''' Little Gray Fry... Please, accept my thanks.
:'''Hysilens:''' I was the only one left after the world was destroyed, and I maintained this lonesome feast with my songs. I have prayed to that {{Rubi|lightless sea|Amphoreus's sky}} for centuries, hoping it would reply to me, yet the emptiness never answered...
:'''Hysilens:''' Thankfully, you arrived as promised, and everyone's wait was not in vain.
:{{Диалог|Стрелка}} Your long wait must have felt like torture.
::'''Hysilens:''' To see a single trace of light in the abyss of futility was already my greatest consolation. When compared to those who have been forgotten... I have no right to complain about my torment.
::Are you still holding it together?
::'''Hysilens:''' Even though madness claws at my mind, my sword stays sharp, my hands agile. If I can uphold this last battlefield, clarity is but an afterthought.
::Your song is beautiful.
:{{Диалог|Стрелка}} Are you still holding it together?
::'''Hysilens:''' Even though madness claws at my mind, my sword stays sharp, my hands agile. If I can uphold this last battlefield, clarity is but an afterthought.
::Your song is beautiful.
:{{Диалог|Стрелка}} Your song is beautiful.
:'''Hysilens:''' Thank you, final audience of mine... Heh. This is probably the last praise I'll ever hear in my life.
:'''Hysilens:''' Now... You and I will walk towards the end of this world.
:'''Hysilens:''' The heroes have waited for this moment for far too long. Let us use our blades to testify our resolve.
:'''Hysilens:''' O prisoner of the seas, Theoros carrying thirty million cycles' of sin, slave of the Erudition...
:'''Hysilens:''' Show yourself! The Deliverer has returned, and the time of your execution draws near.
:'''Lygus:''' I see an awakened human who has mistakenly taken fallacies as truths, and has returned to the cave to try to bring {{MC|м=his|ж=her}} friends into the sunlight {{MC|ж=she|м=he}} once bathed in...
:'''Lygus:''' Alas, prisoners will always be prisoners, blind to the very chains that bind them.
:'''Lygus:''' As the only other existence with free will in this world, I express regret toward your choice, but I shall retain your right to express yourself. After all, every actor should have a final line before they bow out.
:{{Диалог|Стрелка}} It's time to end everything.
::'''Lygus:''' I eagerly look forward to it. The last dusk this world will ever see shall become the climax that decides the fate of the cosmos. Oh, what an appropriate end.
::'''Lygus:''' The Amphorean demigods used every ounce of their strength to constrain me here, yet regrettably...
::The demigods defeated you, clown.
::'''Lygus:''' Allow me to correct your statement: "constrain" does not mean "defeated," and for heroes like yourself, that nuance could make all the difference...
::For a narrator, you're awfully talkative.
:{{Диалог|Стрелка}} The demigods defeated you, clown.
::'''Lygus:''' Allow me to correct your statement: "constrain" does not mean "defeated," and for heroes like yourself, that nuance could make all the difference...
::For a narrator, you're awfully talkative.
:{{Диалог|Стрелка}} For a narrator, you're awfully talkative.
:'''Lygus:''' Trust me. This will be the final scene. The last dusk this world will ever see shall become the climax that decides the fate of the cosmos. What an appropriate end.
:'''Lygus:''' My cognition resides in the Exomyth. It is pointless to defeat my avatar, projected into the experiment. My body is the shadow cast on the wall by the fire, and my words are lingering echoes within the cave.
:{{tx}}
{{Dialogue End}}

===Face Lygus{{subst:void|<!--104061202-->}}===
{{Dialogue Start}}
----
:{{tx}}
----
:'''Lygus:''' Then, within the infinity nurtured by that constant, a new universe shall bud in the chaos. A universe that cannot be predicted... and not shackled by the Erudition.
:'''Lygus:''' As the first prisoner to awaken in the cave, I must lead the others who are blind back onto the right path and reach true sunlight.
:'''Lygus:''' Do you understand me now? As Khaslana stated, "Destruction" is not the process, but the outcome...
:'''Lygus:''' It is revolution through complete annihilation... and the grand rebirth after all has been reduced to ash.
:'''Hysilens:''' ...
:{{Диалог|Стрелка}} I'll never agree with your views.
:{{Диалог|Стрелка}} That's not a reason for you to toy with fate.
:{{Диалог|Стрелка}} Shut it! That's not what Phainon believed at all.
:'''Hysilens:''' The Amphoreans already answered long ago: be it as a tiny fish destined to be swallowed, or as a giant whale poised for a magnificent descent...
:{{tx}}
{{Dialogue End}}

